WEBVTT

00:00:00.191 --> 00:00:02.845
Four engineers. Four months.

00:00:02.865 --> 00:00:06.768
That's what a project took us in 2021.

00:00:06.788 --> 00:00:11.485
Last year, my team shipped a project about the same size:

00:00:11.235 --> 00:00:13.463
TWO engineers. ONE month.

00:00:13.483 --> 00:00:16.659
Call it 8 TO 16 TIMES faster.

00:00:16.409 --> 00:00:21.147
Nobody worked longer hours. Nobody typed faster.

00:00:20.897 --> 00:00:24.969
What changed is what engineers actually DO all day.

00:00:24.719 --> 00:00:29.729
In my team, engineers spend less of their day writing code,

00:00:29.479 --> 00:00:33.659
and more of it reviewing code, aligning requirements,

00:00:33.409 --> 00:00:36.924
and setting GUARDRAILS — the JUDGMENT work.

00:00:36.674 --> 00:00:38.657
One more thing changed.

00:00:38.407 --> 00:00:42.677
In 2021, if we needed a new framework,

00:00:42.427 --> 00:00:46.234
delivery slowed down while people went off and learned it.

00:00:45.984 --> 00:00:48.434
Nobody does that anymore.

00:00:48.184 --> 00:00:50.674
You learn it WHILE YOU BUILD.

00:00:50.664 --> 00:00:52.712
Same week. Same task.

00:00:52.462 --> 00:00:55.352
So here is my working theory:

00:00:55.102 --> 00:00:58.452
AI didn't make engineers faster.

00:00:58.202 --> 00:00:59.285
It CHANGED THE JOB.

00:00:59.035 --> 00:01:02.708
That's what I keep coming back to as a manager:

00:01:02.458 --> 00:01:08.268
my team's structure, my planning, the way engineers grow here —

00:01:08.018 --> 00:01:10.899
all of it was designed for THE OLD JOB.

00:01:10.649 --> 00:01:14.139
So the question isn't "how much faster can we go."

00:01:13.889 --> 00:01:18.719
It is: does the way I run this team still match the job

00:01:18.469 --> 00:01:22.400
my engineers are ACTUALLY DOING now?
